<title>USA: Hilton bid lifts ITT shrs out of 5-mos funk.</title>
<headline>Hilton bid lifts ITT shrs out of 5-mos funk.</headline>
<byline>Brendan Intindola</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>It took Hilton Hotel Corp's $55 per share hostile bid for ITT Corp and the ensuing leap in the target's stock price to make ITT shares a winner, though they still lag far behind market gains posted by its suitor in the past year.</p>
<p>Since December 20, 1995, when shares of ITT began trading as one of three spin-offs from the old ITT, the stock was off 13.4 percent, as of Monday.</p>
<p>But Tuesday's 14-1/2 gain to 57-1/8, driven by the bid, pushed ITT into positive ground, making the stock a 13.1 percent gainer from its first day of trade.</p>
<p>Hilton stock, meanwhile, is up 87 percent over the period.</p>
